.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Miami WR Malachi Toney 'really close' to return after ankle surgery, coach says","description":"Miami star wide receiver Malachi Toney is about a week and a half from returning from surgery for a high ankle sprain, coach Mario Cristobal told \"The Pat McAfee Show.\"","published":"2026-11-20T19:00:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50542494/malachi-toney-nearing-return-ankle-surgery-coach-says","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Draft buzz: Interest in Oklahoma State's Drew Mestemaker could spur draft trade","description":"If the Titans or Chargers wind up with the No. 1 selection and stick with their franchise quarterbacks, interest in Oklahoma State's Drew Mestemaker could lead to a team seeking to trade up for the top overall pick.","published":"2026-11-20T21:59:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50541939/draft-buzz-mestemaker-spur-auction-no-1-pick","type":"Story","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-20T15:55:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5218506/brauntae-johnson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brauntae_Johnson"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Brauntae Johnson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brauntae_Johnson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-19T03:29:12Z","intro":"Brauntae Ladarries Johnson, formerly known as Tae Johnson, is an American college football safety for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Johnson attended North Side High School in Fort Wayne, Indiana. He played wide receiver in high school and finished his career with 139 receptions for 2,286 yards and 41 touchdowns. He committed to the University of Notre Dame to play college football. Johnson also played basketball in high school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his first year at Notre Dame in 2024, Johnson missed time after undergoing foot surgery prior to the season. He returned from the injury to play in three games and redshirted. He entered his redshirt freshman season in 2025 as a backup before taking over as starting free safety against Arkansas."}]}}